Answer: Curly braces group multiple statements into one block so that all of them execute during each iteration.

```java
for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
System.out.println("String Stack");
System.out.println("Technologies Private Limited");
}
```

Both statements are executed five times.

Answer: A variable declared inside the for loop exists only within that loop block. Example:

```java
for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
System.out.println(i);
}
```

After control comes out of the loop, that i is no longer available. It is local to the loop block.

