Answer: In a for loop, initialization, condition, and increment/decrement are normally written together in the loop header.

```java
for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++)
```

In a while loop, these parts are written separately.

```java
int i = 1;
while (i <= 5) {
i++;
}
```

The fundamental looping concept remains the same.

