import java.util.Scanner;
class GCD {
public static void main(String[] args) {
Scanner scan = new Scanner(System.in);
int m = scan.nextInt();
int n = scan.nextInt();
while (n != 0) {
int remainder = m % n;
m = n;
n = remainder;
}
int gcd = m;
System.out.println(gcd);
}
}
```

Sample Input 1: 2 4 Output: 2 Sample Input 2: 16 100 Output: 4 The loop continues as long as n != 0. When n becomes 0, the current value of m is the GCD.
